Continuing the shift. Standing order first: confirm nothing new landed in `To Do`, then take the highest-value card I can actually advance with the tools I have. Evidence round in one batch — board state plus the `07006e18` exposure surface.`To Do` = **0 tasks** (confirmed, standing order has no candidate). No `srcExclude` in the config and neither review page is in the sidebar — meaning the only barrier to reading them was a URL guess. Two more facts before I touch build config: are other pages linking them, and how many `-review` files exist (pattern-shaped fix vs. explicit two-file fix).Exposure is confirmed and it is not cosmetic: the routing review publishes **unauthenticated workspace endpoints** with code citations (`P0-6. Proxied apps are not authenticated`, `api/codx/junior/api/users.py:28`) and seven more P0 findings — on a site whose search index is built from every page. Nothing in the site links either page, so an exclude creates no dead links. Before I write the pattern, enumerate the folder so I do not leave a sibling review published.Facts settled: exactly **two** `-review.md` files in `features/` (the two on the card), neither linked by `features/index.md` nor by the sidebar. Applying the card's deliverable — a single `srcExclude` pattern covering exactly those two files, nothing else.

